<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Familiar</h1>
<p>A familiar is a creature bound to serve you. The one known today is the 
necromancers' golem.
</p><p><b>The golem.</b> Necromancers of level 20 or more can ask Dalmar, in the 
Necromancers' guild, to create a golem. He wants three things first: a dark 
elf's adamantium bracer, the nectar of a flower that grows only in the arctic, 
and an amethyst. Bring him all three, and he performs the ritual. Then whisper 
to your golem 'Serve me', and it bonds to you. It asks what you want to call 
it: give it the name you will command it by.
</p><p><b>Name it wisely.</b> Naming a familiar inappropriately will cost you the 
ability to own one. Don't name it after a player or a monster, or anything 
questionable. If in doubt, choose another name.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
